# Opt113 (2026-10-31, config LO; inert unless set): STRATA_PF_FOLD_SHARED=1 (needs STRATA_PF_GROUP > 1) parks each lockstep chunk's MoE partial sum with the
# gated shared-expert term already added (S = resident rows + sigm(sg) * shared), so the group no longer keeps the shared term (T x N fp32) and its gate (T
# floats) per chunk, and the final combine is S + the Mac rows. bytes_needed and group_extra_bytes count two buffers less per grouped chunk: the prompt's
# card loan falls 1390 -> 1289 slots at 33K (G = 6, 2820-token chunks), every one a resident expert back on the 3090; two device copies less per chunk-layer.
# Numerics: (resident + shared) + Mac instead of (resident + Mac) + shared, fp32 association only.
# Measured (ABBA vs config LN, fresh restart per arm): 33K 989.7 -> 996.5 tok/s (+0.69 %), 8K 840.4 -> 851.0 (+1.26 %), 2.5K 283.6 -> 285.6.
