 // group; each extra chunk keeps its own residual stream R (T x D fp32) and QSA step table on the device.  STRATA_PF_GROUP_NOFUSE=1 also unfuses the layer-boundary
 // write+norm at G=1 (the exactness A/B: the group has to unfuse it, another chunk's turn comes between the write and the next norm).
+// Opt113 STRATA_PF_FOLD_SHARED=1 (needs STRATA_PF_GROUP > 1): the lockstep group parks each chunk's MoE partial sum with the gated shared term already
+// added (S = resident rows + sigm(sg) * shared) instead of three buffers (S, SH = shared, SG = gate), so the final combine is S + Mac rows: two T x N fp32
+// buffers + T floats less per grouped chunk in the borrowed region (~97 cache slots at a 2820-token chunk, G = 6) and two device copies less per chunk-layer.
+// The sum is (resident + shared) + Mac instead of (resident + Mac) + shared: fp32 association only.
+inline bool pf_fold_shared() {
+    static const bool on = [] { const char* v = std::getenv("STRATA_PF_FOLD_SHARED"); return v != nullptr && std::atoi(v) != 0; }();
+    return on;
